	(text "DIR = -IOR (low: CF -> bus)\n-CFOE = -IOR AND -IOW\nACTK sinks the ACT LED"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 271.78 148.59 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0e34d93d-5907-5be4-bf14-8092a9c5ad69")
	)
	(text "U4 gate 2: -CFRESET =\n-RESET AND -SRST\n(bus reset or latch bit 3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 218.44 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "182b2747-fd21-5863-91f6-8e994f806a49")
	)
	(text "1. Two I/O ports. P8 (write): 74LS175 latch U3 - bits 0-2 = the ATA task-file register (CF DA0-2), bit 3 = CF reset\n   (1 = held in reset). P9 (read/write): the selected ATA register, 8-bit True IDE, through the 74LS245 U5.\n2. Decode: 74LS138 U1 on IO-ADDR0-2, enabled by IO-ADDR3 (Y0 = port 8, Y1 = port 9). 74LS32 U2 ORs each port select\n   with -IO-WR / -IO-RD, so -IOR, -IOW and the latch clock are low only during the bus strobe for this card's port\n   (the microcode sets IOADDR two steps before the strobe and holds it through the strobe).\n3. -CS0 (J1 pin 37) is tied LOW and -CS1 (pin 38) HIGH: the strobes alone define every cycle. Gating -CS0 with the\n   port-9 decode would release it on the same clock edge as -IO-RD at the end of an INP, a gate delay BEFORE -IOR\n   rises, breaking the CF chip-select hold time (t9) on the data-register reads that advance its sector buffer.\n4. The CF card sits in a commercial CF-to-IDE adapter on the 40-pin header J1. The adapter is powered from J2\n   (floppy-style 4-pin: 1 = +5 V, 2 and 3 = GND, 4 = +12 V, not used) or, with JP1 fitted, from IDE pin 20 for\n   adapters that take their power there.\n5. Pull-ups: CF D0-7 (RN1: an empty adapter reads $FF, which the ROM driver treats as 'no card'), IORDY, -PDIAG,\n   -DASP; -DMACK held inactive; CSEL grounded (master).\n6. LEDs: PWR; ACT = any port-9 access (the buffer enable); DASP = the CF's own activity/busy pin.\n7. SRST (U3 Q3, latch bit 3 true output) is a named net with no other connection (a probe point).\nTheory of operation: docs/cards/cf.md. Circuit source: cf_netlist.py (edit it, then re-run build.sh)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "291f74a3-63c4-529d-9a7e-88697c9d3489")
	)
	(text "Unused bus pins carry no-connect flags. The card uses DATA0-7, IO-ADDR0-3, -IO-RD,\n-IO-WR, -RESET and the six VCC / six GND pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 127 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2e364d34-ab5d-508d-99cd-69cd7ccf4ac7")
	)
